    "title": "L1 m=4, h=3 Euler quotient factorization",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For every surviving official m=4,h=3 valuation, put V=nu U+XU'. Eliminating D' between the domain derivative and Wronskian equation gives D(2aR+3b)V=H(R^3+aR+b)-4alpha U. The eliminant has H(0)!=0, and if h=deg H then V has exact degree p+h-4, between p-4 and p-nu-1. This exposes at most three top Euler-coefficient cancellations but does not exclude a remaining valuation, count components, or close L1.",
